{
  "_comment": "DESIGN.md §3, §8, §9. Waves 1-25 authored; the scaling factors apply only past wave 25, which the Final Showdown makes academic. Boss waves carry only their escort here - the boss is drawn from bossBank at run time (§3.4). All placeholders.",
  "buildPhaseSeconds": 30,
  "bossEveryNWaves": 5,
  "showdown": {
    "_comment": "§3.3, replaced. The attrition endgame is gone. The last monster wave is afterWave; clearing it moves every surviving army into the cross arena for a free-for-all. approachDepth is the open ground between a player's build grid and the centre square, so a spoke is buildZone.depth + approachDepth long and the centre is buildZone.width on a side. dampening scales healing, summon HP and crowd-control durations down by perSecond per second once graceSeconds have passed, so a fight cannot run forever. All placeholders.",
    "afterWave": 25,
    "countdownSeconds": 3,
    "approachDepth": 2,
    "centre": {
      "_comment": "KING OF THE HILL. Whichever army has the MOST living bodies inside the centre square holds it, and every one of that army’s bodies - wherever it is standing - deals damageDealt more damage and takes damageTaken less. A tie is held by everyone tied, so contesting it is never worse than conceding it. Without this the arena rewards exactly one strategy: mass the slowest, longest-ranged units you can afford, let the other three fight, and walk in to mop up. A reason to stand in the middle is a reason to own a front line. Percentages, in the same convention as an ability’s modify effect: 0.5 is +50%, -0.5 is -50%.",
      "damageDealt": 0.5,
      "damageTaken": -0.5
    },
    "_sightNote": "LINE OF SIGHT. The arena is a cross, and the four corners of its bounding square are not arena: nothing stands there and nothing walks there. With this on they are not transparent either - a body cannot shoot through one, so the back of the south spoke cannot draw a bead on the back of the east spoke across the gap between them. Off, the corners are glass, and a long enough gun covers two spokes from a standing start while nothing can walk to it. A switch rather than a constant so the difference can be measured rather than assumed.",
    "lineOfSight": true,
    "acquire": {
      "_comment": "How far a unit looks for something to fight in the arena, edge to edge in tiles: its own reach plus margin, never less than minimum. Nothing looks across the whole board - a unit with nothing inside this walks at the centre instead, which is what makes four armies converge rather than each pick a duel from thirty tiles away. The lane's equivalent is lane.monsterAcquireRange. Placeholders.",
      "margin": 2,
      "minimum": 3
    },
    "dampening": {
      "graceSeconds": 30,
      "perSecond": 0.01
    }
  },
  "maxConcurrentMonsters": 30,
  "enrage": {
    "_comment": "Additive, not compounding: multiplier = 1 + ratePerSecond * secondsEnraged. rate 0.03 is derived from the doc's worked example (60s in = 2.8x). Applies to monster damage, move speed and attack speed - never to HP.",
    "delaySeconds": 60,
    "ratePerSecond": 0.03,
    "cap": 6.0
  },
